{
  "summary": "Astrophysicist Adam Frank explains that humanity is entering an era where hard data will soon answer the 2,500-year-old question of whether alien civilizations exist. Furthermore, the ancient debate over whether Earth is unique has been settled by the discovery that planets are everywhere, invalidating older theories that predicted planetary systems should be exceptionally rare.",
  "topics": [
