      "title": "Historical Theories of Planet Formation",
      "description": "At the turn of the 20th century, a prominent theory held that planets formed when two stars passed close to each other, gravitationally extracting material—a mechanism so rare it would result in planets around only one in a trillion stars.",
      "timestamp": "00:01:59"
    }
  ],
  "speaker_background": [
    "Adam Frank: Astrophysicist interested in the evolution of star systems and the search for alien civilizations in our universe"
